§ `Victorian workers' compensation indexation notice, 1 July 2026 -- shared terms`

§§ `The two Acts, and the two columns`

-- The Gazette carries one notice per Act. The deposit does not say which Act governs a particular injury or claim (that is
-- in the Acts' transitional provisions, not deposited), so the Act is always an input.
DECLARE `Governing Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013`
    `the Accident Compensation Act 1985`

-- Each table row prints two figures, under the headings "Rate before 1 July 2026" and "Rate from 1 July 2026" (lines 28-29,
-- 408-409). The notice states that weekly payments "are varied on 1 July each year" (lines 18, 398) and the amounts are
-- indexed annually, so the "before" column is read as the figures for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026 and the "from" column as
-- the figures for 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 (wcin-dates.l4).
DECLARE `Notice column` IS ONE OF
    `the rate before 1 July 2026`
    `the rate from 1 July 2026`

-- One printed row: the figure in each column, as printed. No figure is recomputed from the indices (the rounding rules are in
-- the Acts).
DECLARE `Printed pair` HAS
    `printed before 1 July 2026` IS A NUMBER
    `printed from 1 July 2026`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the amount before` IS A NUMBER, `the amount from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`printed as` `the amount before` `then` `the amount from` MEANS
    `Printed pair` WITH
        `printed before 1 July 2026` IS `the amount before`
        `printed from 1 July 2026`   IS `the amount from`

GIVEN `the column` IS A `Notice column`, `the pair` IS A `Printed pair`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount in` `the column` `of` `the pair` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the column`
    WHEN `the rate before 1 July 2026` THEN `the pair`'s `printed before 1 July 2026`
    WHEN `the rate from 1 July 2026`   THEN `the pair`'s `printed from 1 July 2026`

§§ `Questions the notice does not answer`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that can reach a gap answers `not covered`, with one of these reasons.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the day is outside 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027, the two years the notice's columns cover`
    `the facts given are inconsistent`
    `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`
    `the notice prints no maximum weekly payment for this entitlement period, work capacity and claim`
    `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`
    `the notice prints no maximum for this impairment band, and the Act's formula that combines its amounts is not deposited`
    `the notice prints no share of the lump sum for this family, only a maximum: the Act, not deposited, divides it`
    `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
    `the notice prints only an amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation here, not a maximum`
    `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
    `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only where the distance is more than 100 km`
    `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only for the family of a severely injured worker immediately hospitalised after the injury`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

-- The printed figure in the column that an `Answer` names, or the reason there is none.
GIVEN `the column answer` IS AN `Answer` `Notice column`, `the pair` IS A `Printed pair`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the printed figure for` `the column answer` `from` `the pair` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the column answer`
    WHEN `answered` `the column`  THEN `answered` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` `the pair`)
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap`  THEN `not covered` `the gap`

§§ `Rows that state their own arithmetic`

-- Several weekly payment rows print a maximum and then say what is taken off it: "Maximum weekly payments – less worker's
-- current weekly earnings" (2013 Act s 161(b)(ii), line 500), "Maximum weekly payment – less 80% of worker's current weekly
-- earnings" (s 162(b)(ii), line 507), "... less 90% of the worker's current weekly earnings" (1985 Act s 93B(1)(a)(ii),
-- line 197). Such a row is encoded as a ceiling: the printed maximum less that fraction of the worker's current weekly
-- earnings. A row with no "less" has a fraction of 0.
DECLARE `Ceiling row` HAS
    `provision`                                   IS A STRING
    `printed maximum`                             IS A `Printed pair`
    `fraction of current weekly earnings taken off` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `provision` IS A STRING, `the maximum` IS A `Printed pair`, `the fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Ceiling row`
`the ceiling row` `provision` `prints` `the maximum` `less` `the fraction` MEANS
    `Ceiling row` WITH
        `provision`                                     IS `provision`
        `printed maximum`                               IS `the maximum`
        `fraction of current weekly earnings taken off` IS `the fraction`

-- READING: "less" cannot take a ceiling below nothing; a ceiling that the subtraction would make negative is read as 0.
GIVEN `the row` IS A `Ceiling row`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`, `current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling under` `the row` `in` `the column` `with current weekly earnings of` `current weekly earnings` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`the row`'s `printed maximum`)
           MINUS (`the row`'s `fraction of current weekly earnings taken off` TIMES `current weekly earnings`))

-- The weekly payment after the ceiling: the uncapped entitlement (worked out under the Act, an input) or the ceiling,
-- whichever is less.
GIVEN `the uncapped amount` IS A NUMBER, `the ceiling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `the uncapped amount` `and the ceiling` `the ceiling` MEANS min `the uncapped amount` `the ceiling`

§§ `Facts both notices ask about`

-- The entitlement periods are the Acts' (their length and the percentages paid in each are in the Acts, not deposited);
-- the notices print a maximum weekly payment for each (lines 173-251, 496-530).
DECLARE `Entitlement period` IS ONE OF
    `the first entitlement period`
    `the second entitlement period`
    `after the second entitlement period`

-- The minimum earnings rows (2013 Act ss 164(1)(c), 165(4)(a), 166(1)(d), lines 518-530; 1985 Act ss 93CA(1)(c),
-- 93CD(4)(a), 93CDA(1)(d), lines 233-254), named by the notice's own words.
DECLARE `Minimum earnings row` IS ONE OF
    `continuing weekly payments for an incapacity arising from surgery (s 164(1)(c), or s 93CA(1)(c))`
    `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work (s 165(4)(a), or s 93CD(4)(a))`
    `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work under s 165 or s 93CD(4)(a) (s 166(1)(d), or s 93CDA(1)(d))`

-- The deemed pre-injury average weekly earnings rows (2013 Act s 153(5), s 544 and Schedule 2, lines 719-733; 1985 Act
-- s 5A(5), s 100B and Schedule 1A, lines 320-336). Both Schedules use the same item numbers.
DECLARE `Pre-injury earnings item` IS ONE OF
    `Schedule item 1, column 3, paragraph (c): where no rate is applicable`
    `Schedule item 10, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at the time of completion of the course`
    `Schedule item 11, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at a primary or secondary school at the time of completion of secondary school`

DECLARE `Impairment kind` IS ONE OF
    `a permanent impairment`
    `a psychiatric impairment`

-- How the impairment benefit rating is described, which the 2013 Act notice's s 211(2)(b) and (c)(ii) rows turn on
-- (lines 534-547). What makes a rating "modified" is in the Act, not deposited.
DECLARE `Rating description` IS ONE OF
    `a whole person impairment`
    `a modified whole person impairment`
    `a spinal impairment`
    `a modified spinal impairment`

-- The figures the notice prints for an impairment band: the provision and every amount printed in the row, in order. The
-- rows of ss 211(2)(b)-(e), 212(b)-(d), 213 and 214A print two or three amounts without labels.
DECLARE `Impairment figures` HAS
    `provision` IS A STRING
    `amounts`   IS A LIST OF NUMBER

DECLARE `Non-economic loss limit` IS ONE OF
    `more than one injury suffered on the same occasion`
    `more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury`

DECLARE `Head of damages` IS ONE OF
    `pecuniary loss`
    `pain and suffering`

DECLARE `Damages figures` HAS
    `provision`     IS A STRING
    `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum`   IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Dependant kind` IS ONE OF
    `a dependent partner`
    `a dependent child`

-- The headings of the weekly pension rows: "During the first 13 weeks", "After first 13 weeks until the end of three years"
-- (a partner) and "After first 13 weeks until child ceases to be eligible" (a child) (lines 72-145, 456-492).
DECLARE `Pension period` IS ONE OF
    `during the first 13 weeks`
    `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`
    `after the end of three years`

-- A weekly pension row: its provision, its own words, its figures, and how many share it equally (1 unless the row says
-- "in equal shares").
DECLARE `Pension row` HAS
    `provision`            IS A STRING
    `the notice's words`   IS A STRING
    `printed figures`      IS A `Printed pair`
    `shared equally among` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `provision` IS A STRING, `the words` IS A STRING, `the figures` IS A `Printed pair`, `sharers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pension row`
`the pension row` `provision` `reading` `the words` `prints` `the figures` `shared by` `sharers` MEANS
    `Pension row` WITH
        `provision`            IS `provision`
        `the notice's words`   IS `the words`
        `printed figures`      IS `the figures`
        `shared equally among` IS `sharers`

-- What a weekly pension question answers: the row, the printed figure in the column, and one dependant's part of it.
DECLARE `Pension figure` HAS
    `provision`          IS A STRING
    `the notice's words` IS A STRING
    `printed amount`     IS A NUMBER
    `my equal share`     IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the row answer` IS AN `Answer` `Pension row`, `the column answer` IS AN `Answer` `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
`the pension figure for` `the row answer` `in` `the column answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the column answer`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the row answer`
        WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
        WHEN `answered` `the row` THEN
            `answered` (`the pension figure of` `the row` `in` `the column`)

GIVEN `the row` IS A `Pension row`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH A `Pension figure`
`the pension figure of` `the row` `in` `the column` MEANS
    `Pension figure` WITH
        `provision`          IS `the row`'s `provision`
        `the notice's words` IS `the row`'s `the notice's words`
        `printed amount`     IS `the printed amount`
        `my equal share`     IS (`the printed amount` DIVIDED BY (`the row`'s `shared equally among`))
    WHERE
        `the printed amount` MEANS `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`the row`'s `printed figures`)

§§ `Counting dependants`

-- A count of people must be a whole number, not negative.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a count of people` n IF
        n AT LEAST 0
    AND FLOOR n EQUALS n
